### Customizing Text

We can style text with by using the `style.text()` function. This gives us many customization
possibilities for any text we target. For example, the `humidity` column below has green, bolded text
in a custom font.

::: {#1bf31cd4 .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
gt_weather.tab_style(
    style=style.text(color="green", font="Times New Roman", weight="bold"),
    locations=loc.body(columns="humidity")
)
```

