### Using a predicate function

For more flexibility, pass a function to `fn=`. The function receives the raw cell value and should
return `True` to apply the style. Missing values (`NaN` in Pandas) are normalized to `None` before
being passed to your function, so `x is None` works reliably.

::: {#36cd6e7a .cell execution_count=17}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(
    GT(
        exibble[["num", "char", "currency", "row", "group"]],
        rowname_col="row",
        groupname_col="group"
    )
    .tab_style_body(
        style=style.text(color="red"),
        fn=lambda x: x is None,
    )
    .sub_missing(missing_text="NA")
)
```

