### Expanding matches with `targets=`

By default, only the matched cell itself is styled (`targets="cell"`). You can expand the styling to
entire rows or columns that contain a match:

- `targets="row"`: style the full row of each match
- `targets="column"`: style the full column of each match
- `targets=["row", "column"]`: both

::: {#9849e02e .cell execution_count=21}
``` {.python .cell-code}
